=== STEP 1 · replay: write a log, replay it, compare with a tolerance =====
  log: 600 segments, 9.6 MB (replay_log.jsonl)
  re-run of the same code      : 0/600 segments differ, 0 not bit-identical
  refactor (float32, reordered): 0/600 differ beyond tol, but 600 are not bit-identical (max diff 9.7e-05)
  behaviour change (add AEB)   : 12/600 segments differ -> open them: [57, 67, 73, 123, 173]
  'fastest' replay             : 0 late, 0 dropped frames (deadlines do not exist)
  real-time replay             : 585 late + 583 dropped of 60009 frames; 374/600 segments change
  (0.1+0.2)+0.3 = 0.6000000000000001   0.1+(0.2+0.3) = 0.6
  -> evidence/replay.json

=== STEP 2 · scenarios: mine the logs, build the grid, validate the simulator 
  worked example: gap 12 m, closing 5 m/s -> TTC = 2.40 s, required decel = 1.04 m/s^2
  mined 614 lead-braking events out of 9610 trajectories (6.4 %); peak lead decel p50 -2.5, p99 -4.2 m/s^2
  hardest braking any logged human applied (99.9th percentile): 3.6 m/s^2; the actuator can do 9
  grid 60 gaps x 45 closing speeds = 2700 cells; 13 % of the grid needs braking harder than any logged human ever did
  validation t_react=0.0: full-brake collides in 3.6 % of cells, physics says 3.6 % unavoidable; mismatching cells away from the frontier: 0
  validation t_react=0.6: full-brake collides in 10.2 % of cells, physics says 10.2 % unavoidable; mismatching cells away from the frontier: 0
  IDM, t_react 0.0 -> 0.6 s: collision area 3.6 % -> 10.2 %
  -> evidence/scenarios.json

